1.	Overview

Before starting please note the following:

a. Motoring Expenses uses the mileage and dates entered when the motorist enters personal fuel data to estimate future servicing by date and mileage.
b. The application will produce error messages when using new files if not enough fuel entries and servicing entries are made. It also needs servicing intervals to be entered.
c. The application expects the mileage and dates to increase when fuel and servicing data is entered, otherwise errors may occur. (Mileage should not reduce for a later date!) 
d. The application functions best after a number of servicing and fuel entries have been made.
e. The current vehicle's databases are sorted and compressed on exiting the program. The databases are sorted by mileage except the reminder database which is sorted by date.

Motoring expenses is an application designed to help the average motorist 
keep track of his monthly motoring expenditure.  It will supply reports and statistics 
and help remind the motorist of when servicing of the vehicle is due.  It can keep 
track of a number of vehicles and can produce a personal fuel consumption graph.  
Obviously the author can take no responsibility for any loss of data or incorrect 
servicing information, the program is only an aid.  Any problems should be 
reported to the author who will try and rectify the problem. 

